## Root Cause
The code concatenates user input directly into a SQL query, making it vulnerable to SQL injection attacks.

## Explanation
The patch uses parameterized queries to safely include user input without the risk of SQL injection. This is achieved by replacing the concatenation with a placeholder that the database will safely replace with the user-provided value.

## Patch
--- a/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
+++ b/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
		where: {
			name: {
-                [Op.like]: '%' + req.body.name + '%'
+                [Op.like]: { [Op.concat]: ['%', req.body.name, '%'] }
			}
		}
